cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Harmonized U.S. Fetal Death Microdata, 1992-2022"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Plutchok
    given-names: Yoel
    email: yoelyehudaplutchok@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A modern, researcher-ready release of harmonized U.S. fetal death microdata
  for cross-year stillbirth research. Spans 29 years (1992-2022, with 2003-2004
  deferred to V2.1) of NCHS public-use fetal death files reconciled into a
  single Parquet file with one stable schema. Three revisions of the Standard
  Report of Fetal Death (1978, 1989, 2003) and staggered state adoption are
  bridged via documented crosswalks. Validation: 74 checks against
  published NCHS/NVSR statistics (55 V1 + 19 V2): 68 byte-exact matches plus
  6 documented differences in V1 detail-cell tabulations (NVSR's proportional
  redistribution of unknown-gestational-age records, and a 43-state cause-of-death
  reporting area vs all-states totals); all 29 per-year counts and 26 per-year
  rates match exactly. Companion
  to the
  U.S. Natality Harmonization Project (Zenodo concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19363074),
  which supplies the live-birth denominators needed for fetal mortality rate
  computation.
keywords:
  - stillbirth
  - fetal death
  - perinatal epidemiology
  - National Vital Statistics System
  - NCHS
  - data harmonization
  - cross-revision
  - 1989 revision
  - 2003 revision
  - public health
  - epidemiology
  - United States
